;; What ci/metrics-gate.clj (jolt metrics:gate) holds the jolt-metrics report to.
;;
;; :critical-free: path prefixes where a CRITICAL finding (a function past a
;; complexity, length, nesting or parameter limit, or a file past the file
;; length limit) or a file jolt-metrics can't read fails the gate. There is no
;; list of accepted criticals: a tree joins once it has none. resources/ still
;; has seven, each a hot path or a fixed native signature (ROADMAP, Metrics).
;;
;; :unused-requires, :unused-private, :unused-public: unused code that stays,
;; each with :why. The gate fails on an unused one missing here and on an entry
;; here that's no longer reported.
{:critical-free ["src/" "tools/" "bench/" "test/" "ci/" "examples/"]
 :unused-requires []
 :unused-private []
 :unused-public []}
